# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every
# platform. The sources are built both natively on Windows and cross-compiled
# on Linux, and the shell scripts under tools/ run inside a Fedora container,
# where a CRLF shebang fails with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M".
#
# Keeping the working tree LF on Windows too, rather than converting on
# checkout, means a file has the same bytes wherever it is opened: MinGW's sed
# and awk silently rewrite CRLF to LF on output, so a mixed-ending file turns a
# one-line edit into a whole-file diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched, whatever they contain.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.qm  binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
